{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>ויחשבה</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and ויחשבה לזונה regarding Tamar, and ויחשבה עלי לשכורה regarding Hannah. This is what R. Yochanan said: 'Let my portion be with one who is suspected yet is innocent.' For Tamar, because Judah suspected her, she merited — and from her emerged Peretz and Zerach, from whom came kings and prophets. Hannah, because Eli suspected her, she merited — and from her emerged Samuel. Because they were suspected as a zonah and as a hired woman, it was accounted to them as righteousness. (R. Asher)"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The attribution א\"א הרא\"ש expands to אא\"ר הרא\"ש — 'my master and teacher, R. Asher'; resolved per standard Ba'al HaTurim citation conventions."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:10.692475937Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}